goals/effect-vitest-canon/SPEC.md:522:| 2026-10-06 | Bound all six native layer hooks in the next resource batch to five seconds. | The installed 4.0.1 adapter forwards this option to layer acquisition and scope-close hooks. These layers construct local platform services; they start no container or server. Four historical EV014 registrations and two newly introduced registrations lacked explicit budgets. Test-body timeouts, property floors and runtime mode are unchanged. Final Node/Bun and package proofs must bind the resulting source. | Revert only these six options if layer construction gains a demonstrated longer lifecycle, then choose and prove an explicit replacement budget. Do not restore implicit unbounded policy. |
goals/effect-vitest-canon/SPEC.md:526:| 2026-10-06 | Preserve the numeric ratchet's baseline-selected metric policy while repairing its misleading property test and documentation. | `diffTotals` deliberately walks baseline keys; its sole production caller passes the full JSDoc inventory and only selected baseline totals. A current-only inventory-volume metric is counted but is not a regression. The old test supplied explicit zero despite its absent-key title; the proposed absent-key increase failed. Retain its exact zero fixture/assertions, name it accurately, test the actual untracked-key boundary, and add the missing success-log oracle. | Revert the test/doc clarification together if the tracked-metric policy changes. Any future union-of-keys implementation must first separate inventory-volume totals from debt metrics and qualify every production caller. Preserve the historical finding ID and failed proposal receipt. |
goals/effect-vitest-canon/SPEC.md:534:| 2026-10-06 | Prepare fourteen existing property-boundary findings in a sibling lane based on qualified resource source, preserving each subject and its original inventory identity. | All 915 unchanged tests pass on Node and Bun before edits. The parent first strengthens optional read errors, native Git tree output, and the actual default model verifier; disjoint writers own the remaining goal/projection and command/property-law cases. A new global census is deferred until existing backlog closure. | Archive the sibling lane if abandoned; otherwise revert each source/ledger disposition together, retaining before tests, injected counterexamples and independent review receipts. |
goals/effect-vitest-canon/SPEC.md:536:| 2026-10-06 | Re-export the existing `parseCard` boundary from the existing Research test kit. | The authored card round-trip must decode actual saved frontmatter through its real public test seam. The original schema decoder already exists; adding one source-only test-facade export avoids a duplicate parser or bypassing package aliases. | Remove the test-only re-export together with the dependent round-trip assertion if that boundary moves; no production implementation or package export map changes. |
goals/effect-vitest-canon/SPEC.md:538:| 2026-10-06 | Prepare C4's fourteen property-boundary dispositions only after the exact calendar issue oracle, preserving old source receipts and historical identities. | A one-argument canonical helper produced 918/919 and TS2555; an interim instance-only SchemaError assertion then passed 919/919 but accepted wrong-field failures. Installed Standard Schema issue formatting plus independently expected created path/messages rejects all three private counterexamples on both runtimes. Final fifteen-path R2 snapshot has 919/919 and qualified direct compiler exit zero; package proof and explicit parent review acceptance remain required before any disposition. The D5 docgen hash supersedes its earlier report only for current qualification, without rewriting that report. | Revert the exact source assertion together with any later qualified fourteen-row disposition; retain both interrupted package receipts and original row preimages. The preparation alone changes no canonical row, baseline or lifecycle gate. |
